<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijayawada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bezawada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijayawada is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the head of the Krishna delta. Known historically as Bezawada, it was a centre of the Vishnukundina dynasty, and it has the hill temple of Kanaka <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durga">Durga</a> and rock-cut cave temples at Undavalli and Mogalrajapuram nearby. The Prakasam Barrage there irrigates much of the delta.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vijayawada.jpg" alt="Vijayawada" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luke John · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prakasham_Barriage,_Vijayawada.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
